# apps/customer_app/.easignore
# EAS archives from the monorepo GIT ROOT, so every path here is git-root-relative.
# Goal: upload ONLY what the customer build needs (apps/customer_app + shared packages/),
# not the whole monorepo. Without complete exclusions EAS uploaded ~304 MB (all the other
# apps + web projects + infra + docs), which failed on upload (ECONNRESET).
#
# Root-level dirs are ANCHORED with a leading "/" so a bare name never strips an identically
# named subdir INSIDE apps/customer_app (e.g. its own components/, lib/, hooks/).

# --- Other apps / web projects (not needed for the customer build) ---
/apps/gatimitra-riderApp/
/apps/merchant_app/
/rider-web/
/cxsite/

# --- Backend / dashboards / web / infra (never needed for a mobile build) ---
/backend/
/dashboard/
/dashboards/
/partnersite/
/services/
/infra/
/docs/
/scripts/
/merchant_db/
/.github/

# --- node_modules anywhere (EAS installs deps on the builder) ---
**/node_modules/

# --- Native dirs: managed workflow; EAS runs expo prebuild ---
/apps/customer_app/android/
/apps/customer_app/ios/

# --- Caches / build artifacts ---
**/.expo/
**/.expo-shared/
**/.gradle/
**/.next/
**/.cache/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/out/
**/tmp/
**/temp/
**/logs/
*.log
*.tgz
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.keystore

# --- Env files (secrets) — keep examples ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- Editor / OS / tests ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/__tests__/
**/*.test.*
**/*.spec.*
**/coverage/
